entral squares (d5 and f5)\n- It opens diagonals for both the kingside bishop (f1) and the queen (d1)\n- It allows for rapid piece development\n- It's the most testing opening, putting immediate pressure on Black\n- It leads to sharp, tactical positions where White can leverage the first-move advantage\n- Historically, it's been the choice of most World Champions for its dynamic winning chances\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e4"}
