d the center\n- Targets f7, Black's most vulnerable square (only defended by the king)\n- Prepares kingside castling (O-O)\n- Maintains flexibility - I can later support with d4, or continue pressure with Ng5\n- Follows classical opening principles: develop pieces, control center, prepare castling\n- The bishop on c4 is particularly strong given Black's f6 pawn doesn't control the e5 square effectively\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
