ot defend both pieces. Even if Black moves the queen, I win the rook on h8. This is a decisive material advantage that should lead to a winning position. The knight on f7 is also protected by being out of immediate danger, and Black has no good way to deal with both threats.\n\nAnswer: N: g5-f7"}
