 material immediately.\n\n5. **Q: d1-h5** - Brings the queen into the attack with check, forcing Black's king to move and creating immediate threats against the exposed king position.\n\nReason: While capturing the rook with N: f7-h8 wins material, the more forcing move is **Q: d1-h5**, which delivers check to the exposed king on g6. This forces Black's king to move (likely Kg7 or Kf6), and then I can follow up with capturing the rook on h8 with my knight on the next move, or continue pressing the attack against the displaced king. This is more forcing and maintains the initiative while keeping all my tactical options open.\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-h5"}
