iss the immediate tactical opportunity.\n\nReason: **Q: f7-f8** is the strongest move because:\n- It gives direct check to the Black king on h7\n- Forces Black's king to move to a worse square (likely g7 or h6)\n- Maintains attacking pressure on the 8th rank\n- The Black rook on f8 square is undefended after my Queen occupies it\n- This continues the attack while Black's pieces remain undeveloped and unable to coordinate a defense\n- It's a forcing move that keeps the initiative and doesn't allow Black time to consolidate\n\nAnswer: Q: f7-f8"}
