\n1 |RWF0|NWF0|BWF0|    |    |RWF1|KWF1|    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a2-a4, P: a2-a3, N: b1-a3, N: b1-c3, P: b2-b4, P: b2-b3, P: c2-c4, P: c2-c3, P: d2-d4, P: d2-d3, P: d7-c8-q, P: d7-c8-n, P: d7-c8-b, P: d7-c8-r, P: d7-d8-q, P: d7-d8-n, P: d7-d8-b, P: d7-d8-r, R: f1-e1, R: f1-d1, P: f2-f4, P: f2-f3, K: g1-h1, P: g2-g4, P: g2-g3, P: h2-h4, P: h2-h3]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I'm playing as White and I notice an extraordinary opportunity - I have a white pawn on d7 (PWF1), which is on the 7th rank deep in Black's territory! This pawn can promote on my next move. Black's king is on g7, and their pieces are somewhat uncoordinated. Black has material advantage with more pieces, but my advanced pawn is a critical asset.\n\nEvaluation: Let me consider the key moves:\n\n1. **P: d7-d8-q (Promote to Queen)** - This creates a new queen on d8, giving me a massive material advantage. The new queen would be on the back rank, threatening multiple pieces and controlling key squares. This is the strongest piece and would immediately shift the balance of power.\n\n2. **P: d7-c8-q (Promote to Queen by capturing)** - This captures the bishop on c8 and promotes, gaining material and a queen. However, d8 seems better positioned.\n\n3. **P: d7-d8-n (Promote to Knight)** - A knight on d8 could give some checks, but a queen is far more powerful in this position.\n\n4. Other pawn moves or piece moves - These are all vastly inferior to promoting my advanced pawn immediately.\n\nReason: Promoting to a queen on d8 is the overwhelming choice. A queen is worth approximately 9 points of material, and placing it on the back rank gives me immediate tactical threats. The queen on d8 would attack the rook on h8, control the 8th rank, and give me winning chances despite being behind in material. This is a game-changing move that I must play immediately.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d8-q"}
