e because:\n- It delivers check to the exposed king on e6\n- The king has limited escape squares (likely d7, d6, d5, f7, or f5)\n- After the king moves, I can continue applying pressure with my well-placed queen\n- It maintains my dominant position and keeps Black on the defensive\n- This forcing move prevents Black from consolidating their position\n\nAnswer: Q: f8-e8"}
