fter **Q: c6-c8+**, the King must move:\n- If Kd7, the Queen controls key escape squares\n- If Ke7, similar situation with the King trapped\n- If Kf7, Kd6, Kf6, Kd5, or Kf5, the King moves further into danger\n\nReason: Q: c6-c8 delivers immediate check to the exposed King on e6, forcing it to move to an even worse position. With the King so centralized and Black's pieces uncoordinated, this check initiates a decisive attack. The Queen from c8 will dominate the board and create unstoppable mating threats.\n\nAnswer: Q: c6-c8"}
