icantly.\n\nReason: N: c3-d5 gives check to the Black king on c5, forcing it to move and allowing me to seize the initiative. The knight would be excellently placed on d5, controlling critical central squares (b4, b6, c7, e7, f6, f4) and restricting Black's king mobility. This forcing move takes advantage of Black's most significant weakness - their exposed king position. After the king moves, I can continue developing with threats and maintain pressure.\n\nAnswer: N: c3-d5"}
