n- Puts immediate pressure on Black's exposed king\n- Gains tempo by forcing Black to respond to the check\n- The knight on c6 would be well-placed, controlling important squares\n- Forces Black into a defensive position where the king must retreat to a potentially worse square\n\nThis check maximizes immediate tactical pressure and exploits Black's king vulnerability.\n\nAnswer: N: e7-c6"}
