ely to b4, c5, or a6/a4), and after the king moves, I can continue to harass it or reposition my knight favorably. An exposed king in the middle of the board is Black's greatest weakness, and I should exploit it immediately with forcing moves. Checks are always worth considering when the opponent's king is vulnerable.\n\nAnswer: N: c6-a5"}
