ing the rook on d8 wins material immediately (a rook is worth about 5 points), giving check with N: c6-b4 is even stronger tactically. It forces Black's king to move from b5, and after the king moves, I can potentially follow up with capturing the rook on d8 or creating further threats. The check maintains tempo and initiative while the exposed Black king position suggests tactical opportunities.\n\nAnswer: N: c6-b4"}
