ter the check, Black's king will be forced to move (likely to a5, a7, or b5), and this will limit Black's options while I maintain the initiative. In endgames with exposed kings, forcing moves like checks are often the most effective way to gain an advantage. The knight on b7 would also be well-placed to continue harassing the king and controlling key squares.\n\nAnswer: N: d8-b7"}
