 is the strongest move. It gives check to the black king on b5, forcing Black to move the king to a worse square. After the king moves, I can continue improving my position with my rooks. The knight on d6 will be excellently centralized, controlling many key squares (b5, b7, c4, e4, f5, f7) and coordinating well with my rooks for a potential mating attack. This forcing move maintains the initiative.\n\nAnswer: N: b7-d6"}
