+** is the strongest choice. It gives check to the Black King on a5, forcing it to move (likely to a4, a6, or b5). The Knight on b7 would be excellently placed, controlling important squares and potentially helping to deliver checkmate. This is more forcing than the Rook moves and creates immediate tactical pressure. The Knight fork pattern and king restriction possibilities make this the most concrete winning attempt.\n\nAnswer: N: d6-b7"}
