n)\n\nThis check forces Black's hand and maintains White's initiative with the active rook.\n\nReason: R: e5-e6 is the strongest move because it gives check, forcing Black's king to move to a potentially worse square. This maintains the initiative and puts maximum pressure on Black's exposed king. Checking moves should always be considered first as they limit the opponent's options. After the king moves, I can continue to hunt it with my rook and knight coordination.\n\nAnswer: R: e5-e6"}
