ves check, forcing Black's King to move (likely to c6, d4, or c5)\n- It activates my Rook to a dominant 5th rank position\n- It maintains pressure and keeps the initiative\n- After the King moves, my Knight on d6 continues to control key squares\n- This maintains maximum winning chances by keeping pieces active and the Black King under pressure\n\nAnswer: R: e4-e5"}
