 gives check, forcing Black's King to move and disrupting any plans\n- It activates my Rook further up the board\n- It maintains pressure and keeps the initiative\n- After the King moves (likely Kd7, Kd5, or Kc7), I can continue to harass the King and potentially cut it off from supporting the passed pawns\n- This move maximizes my winning chances by staying aggressive in the endgame\n\nAnswer: R: e5-e6"}
