 likely win.\n\nReason: R: f5-f1 is the best move because:\n- It gets behind the passed pawn, following the principle "rooks belong behind passed pawns"\n- It prevents c2-c1 promotion\n- It keeps the rook active on the first rank\n- It maintains flexibility to deal with Black\'s other threats\n- From f1, the rook can laterally defend and attack as needed\n\nAnswer: R: f5-f1'}
